WEBVTT

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:26.399
I'm surprised the Ministry's
still letting you walk around free.

00:00:26.566 --> 00:00:28.068
Better enjoy it while you can.

00:00:28.235 --> 00:00:31.530
I expect there's a cell in Azkaban
with your name on it.

00:00:34.115 --> 00:00:37.058
-What'd I tell you? Complete nutter.
-Just stay away from me!

00:00:39.287 --> 00:00:40.692
It's only Malfoy.

00:00:41.957 --> 00:00:43.232
What'd you expect?

00:01:03.770 --> 00:01:04.938
Hi, guys.

00:01:05.105 --> 00:01:06.773
-Hey, Neville.
-Hey there, Neville.

00:01:19.828 --> 00:01:20.841
What is it?

00:01:23.540 --> 00:01:25.733
- What's what?
- That. Pulling the carriage.

00:01:27.627 --> 00:01:29.053
Nothing's pulling the carriage, Harry.

00:01:30.589 --> 00:01:31.939
It's pulling itself, like always.

00:01:46.438 --> 00:01:47.638
You're not going mad.

00:01:51.234 --> 00:01:52.536
I can see them too.

00:01:54.738 --> 00:01:56.254
You're just as sane as I am.

00:02:02.162 --> 00:02:03.425
Everyone, this is Loony Love--

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:08.258
Luna Lovegood.

00:02:12.839 --> 00:02:14.085
What an interesting necklace.

00:02:15.717 --> 00:02:16.896
It's a charm, actually.

00:02:19.262 --> 00:02:20.847
Keeps away the Nargles.

00:02:24.643 --> 00:02:25.784
Hungry.

00:02:26.811 --> 00:02:28.062
I hope there's pudding.

00:02:29.773 --> 00:02:31.218
What's a Nargle?

00:02:31.415 --> 00:02:32.640
No idea.

00:02:46.081 --> 00:02:47.707
Good evening, children.

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:51.711
Now, we have two changes
in staffing this year.

00:02:51.878 --> 00:02:54.623
We're pleased to welcome back
Professor Grubbly-Plank...

00:02:55.090 --> 00:02:57.156
...who'll be taking
Care of Magical Creatures...

00:02:57.602 --> 00:03:00.594
...while Professor Hagrid
is on temporary leave.

00:03:02.138 --> 00:03:05.932
We also wish to welcome our new
Defense Against the Dark Arts teacher...

00:03:06.309 --> 00:03:08.395
...Professor Dolores Umbridge.

00:03:09.813 --> 00:03:13.195
And I'm sure you'll all join me
in wishing the professor good luck.

00:03:14.317 --> 00:03:17.737
Now, as usual, our caretaker, Mr. Filch,
has asked me to remind you--

00:03:30.067 --> 00:03:31.331
She was at my hearing.

00:03:31.928 --> 00:03:33.128
She works for Fudge.

00:03:33.294 --> 00:03:37.918
Thank you, headmaster,
for those kind words of welcome.

00:03:40.385 --> 00:03:44.055
And how lovely to see all your bright...

00:03:44.362 --> 00:03:46.848
...happy faces smiling up at me.

00:03:47.604 --> 00:03:52.605
I'm sure we're all going
to be very good friends.

00:03:52.772 --> 00:03:54.364
-That's likely.
-That's likely.

00:03:57.861 --> 00:04:00.822
The Ministry of Magic
has always considered...

00:04:00.989 --> 00:04:06.219
...the education of young witches
and wizards to be of vital importance.

00:04:06.953 --> 00:04:09.247
Although each headmaster...

00:04:09.414 --> 00:04:13.062
...has brought something new
to this historic school...

00:04:15.795 --> 00:04:21.008
...progress for the sake of progress
must be discouraged.

00:04:22.677 --> 00:04:26.134
Let us preserve
what must be preserved...

00:04:26.681 --> 00:04:29.645
...perfect what can be perfected...

00:04:30.351 --> 00:04:34.014
...and prune practices
that ought to be...

00:04:34.731 --> 00:04:36.034
...prohibited.

00:04:44.032 --> 00:04:45.825
Thank you, Professor Umbridge.

00:04:45.992 --> 00:04:48.161
That really was most illuminating.

00:04:48.328 --> 00:04:52.075
- Illuminating? What a load of waffle.
- What's it mean?

00:04:53.416 --> 00:04:55.595
Magic is forbidden in the corridors....

00:04:55.752 --> 00:04:58.389
It means the Ministry's
interfering at Hogwarts.

00:05:19.108 --> 00:05:20.420
Dean, Seamus.

00:05:21.152 --> 00:05:23.099
- Good holiday?
- All right.

00:05:23.655 --> 00:05:25.095
Better than Seamus', anyway.

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:28.916
Me mum didn't want me
to come back this year.

00:05:29.702 --> 00:05:32.727
-Why not?
-Let me see. Uh, because of you.

00:05:33.694 --> 00:05:36.873
The Daily Prophet's been saying a lot
of things about you and Dumbledore.

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:38.294
What, your mum believes them?

00:05:38.461 --> 00:05:40.380
Nobody was there the night Cedric died.

00:05:40.547 --> 00:05:43.633
I guess you should read the Prophet,
then, like your stupid mother.

00:05:43.800 --> 00:05:47.303
-Don't talk about my mother.
-I'll go at anyone that calls me a liar.

00:05:47.470 --> 00:05:49.563
- What's going on?
- He's mad, is what's going on.

00:05:50.139 --> 00:05:52.956
Do you believe the rubbish he's come out
with about You-Know-Who?

00:05:53.593 --> 00:05:55.061
Yeah. I do.

00:05:56.062 --> 00:05:57.552
Has anyone else
got a problem with Harry?

00:06:07.448 --> 00:06:08.838
-You all right?
-Fine.

00:06:10.034 --> 00:06:11.659
Seamus was bang out of order, mate.

00:06:13.413 --> 00:06:16.176
-But he'll come through, you'll see.
-I said, I'm fine, Ron.

00:06:20.837 --> 00:06:24.027
Right. I'll just leave you
to your thoughts, then.

